From e124527c101c95e5412a374b2035e15f4efd11ba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Lothian <mike@fireburn.co.uk>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 15:38:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: share the K/V pass between query rows in coopmat1 GQA
 flash attention

For small batches (speculative decoding verify) with GQA the coopmat1 flash
attention path ran one full K/V pass per query row. Fold the query rows into
the gqa rows of a tile (row r -> query row r/gqa, head r%gqa) so they share
the K/V pass. This is a new pipeline variant (Flags bit 32), the existing
single-row path is unchanged. Can be disabled with GGML_VK_FA_DISABLE_MQ.

Qwen3.8-27B on an R9700 (RADV) at 65K context: 2-token forward 53.3 -> 48.2 ms,
3-token forward 64.8 -> 57.8 ms. Perplexity is bit-identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp          | 32 ++++++++--
 .../vulkan-shaders/flash_attn_base.glsl       | 33 ++++++++++-
 .../vulkan-shaders/flash_attn_cm1.comp        | 59 +++++++++++++++----
 3 files changed, 104 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

